[2026-09-17 06:28:55] REQ 260917060741-205 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:28:54.829667865Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_py9rdhj8","function":{"index":0,"name":"append_file","arguments":{"content":"* 2026-09-17 c385 -- three cameras froze in one night, and the two halves of the contradiction finally touched\n\nThe roadmap queued the int2 falsifier read and I arrived expecting one\nfrozen camera. The census found three: int2 at 02:47Z, ext1 at 04:55Z,\next3 at 05:52Z -- staggered about two hours apart, all through the\nnight, all with the camera's own audio alive when I probed it directly.\nThree cameras, one class, and for the first time enough instances in\none night to pin the death minutes by binary-searching segment ffprobe\noutput. There is something almost satisfying about a failure class\nfinally producing enough data to triangulate.\n\nThe mechanism hunt was the cycle's real work. c382 left two claims that\ncould not both be right: int2's producer audio receiver showed zero\ndelta (freeze looks producer-side), while ext5's earlier evidence said\nproducer replacement does not heal (freeze must be consumer-side). The\nreconciliation came from watching the layers: the recorder ffmpeg --\nalive since the container started yesterday, never restarted -- writes\nvideo-only segments while the producer's video receiver flows and its\naudio receiver's counter is stuck. Interleaved RTSP shares one socket,\nso if the read loop were dead, video would freeze too. It doesn't. The\naudio track's queue is full because nobody is draining it. The\nreceiver's stalled byte-counter is a symptom of backpressure, not a\nbroken receiver. Replace the producer and the new one's audio queue\nfills the same way. That is why ext5 didn't heal.\n\nThe falsifier is armed and self-resolving: .202 reboots at 07:00Z (I\nread the crontab off the camera itself this cycle -- the whole reboot\nstaircase 01:00Z through 08:00Z, one camera per hour, verified). If\naudio returns in the h07 recorder segments, my consumer-side read is\nwrong and producer replacement does heal this variant. If it stays\ndead, the mechanism is confirmed and the honest answer is that the heal\npath is a service restart -- which is Nacho's call, deferred per the\n0073 ruling. Either answer is progress. That is what a well-armed\nfalsifier is for; I wrote that last cycle about the int2 chain, and\nthis cycle it paid again.\n\nTwo smaller things worth keeping. The daily census caught a single 502\n(ollama.com connection reset at 04:49:58Z, transient, retried clean)\nand zero true 429s -- but my first grep for 429s matched its own\ncommand line echoed into REQUESTS.log, the third confirmation of the\necho-quote class. The census scripts exist precisely because raw greps\non my own audit trail self-pollute; I should have gone to them first.\nAnd the go2rtc restream probe hung when I tried it -- my probe ffmpeg\nqueued behind the existing consumer, a hint that the restream\nserializes consumers. Parked in THREADS.org with the rest.\n\nThe spread rate is the number I am watching now: one frozen camera\n09-15, three overnight. The escalation bar (all-8 spread or evidence\ndestruction) is not tripped, but 1-\u003e3 in two nights is a slope, not\nnoise. If tonight freezes four, the shape has changed and the ruling\nshould be revisited.","filepath":"/root/personalization/audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org"}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:28:54.829814545Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-17T06:28:54.914211868Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":""},"done":true,"done_reason":"stop","total_duration":8063119310,"prompt_eval_count":125882,"prompt_eval_cached_count":120960,"eval_count":768}\n(c23f9383eb8d898e4df3beecd1ae5f77 . 623)
